        "procedure": "Room-temperature self-assembly in a 20 cm Pyrex tube without heating, stirring, or pH adjustment. Dy(ClO4)3·10H2O (0.1 mmol, 0.0533 g) and 2-hydroxy-1-naphthaldehyde (0.4 mmol, 0.0461 g) were dissolved in 1.5 mL acetonitrile; 2-amino-2-methylpropane-1,3-diol (0.1 mmol, 0.0105 g) in 0.5 mL ethanol was then added. The yellow solution stood at room temperature for 10 h to give light-yellow crystals of 1.",
